  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of NNN integers. Find the maximum value of (Aimod  (Aj+Ak))(A_i \\mod (A_j + A_k))(Ai​mod(Aj​+Ak​)) over all possible triplets satisfying 1≤i,j,k≤N1 \\le i, j, k \\le N1≤i,j,k≤N and i,j,ki, j, ki,j,k are pairwise distinct.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN - the size of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum value of (Aimod  (Aj+Ak))(A_i \\mod (A_j + A_k))(Ai​mod(Aj​+Ak​)).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "3≤N≤50003 \\le N \\le 50003≤N≤5000",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\le A_i \\le 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of N2N^2N2 over all test cases does not exceed 500025000^250002."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3\n1 2 3\n3\n1 3 3",
        "output": "2\n3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : We can choose the triplet (i,j,k)=(2,1,3)(i, j, k) = (2, 1, 3)(i,j,k)=(2,1,3) and we get the value of A2mod  (A1+A3)=2mod  4=2A_2 \\mod (A_1 + A_3) = 2 \\mod 4 = 2A2​mod(A1​+A3​)=2mod4=2.\nTest Case 2 : We can choose the triplet (i,j,k)=(3,1,2)(i, j, k) = (3, 1, 2)(i,j,k)=(3,1,2) and we get the value of A3mod  (A1+A2)=3mod  4=3A_3 \\mod (A_1 + A_2) = 3 \\mod 4 = 3A3​mod(A1​+A2​)=3mod4=3."
      }
    ]
  },
